Hericlitus: No man steps in the same river twice, for it is not the same river and he is not the same man
=> END

~ narration
You have arrived at limbo, the space between life and death. To move on to the afterlife, you must build up your boat’s style, sturdiness, and size.
You have six memories from your past life keeping your boat afloat, but you may only take one with you to the afterlife. You must give up the others by the time you leave this place.
Each stage of the journey, you will be offered 3 memories to give up. Each time you give up a memory, you lose the contribution to the style, sturdiness, and size that that memory provides.
Style - Represents how comfortable you will be in the afterlife
Studiness - Represents how much strength and growth you take along to the afterlife
Size - Represents the amount of knowledge you take along to the afterlife
There will be other actions you can choose from as you continue your journey. Here is how it’ll work\:
=> END
